  "deprecation": {
    "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.10.09.17.42.46/orleindustries.ipgkit.web.customer.1.0.0-rc.6.json#deprecation",
    "message": "Security: upgrade to 1.0.0-rc.7. In 1.0.0-rc.6 and earlier, POST /payments accepted apiConsumerId and paymentLinkId from the request body, so one API consumer could create a payment attributed to another consumer (who then received a validly signed payment.created webhook) or attach it to another consumer's payment link (P77). Fixed in 1.0.0-rc.7. rc.7 also carries breaking contract changes and three migrations - see the CHANGELOG and docs/upgrading-to-v1.md section 15.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other",
      "Legacy",
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
  "description": "The IpgKit citizen account surface — register, sign in, password reset, email confirmation, two-factor and profile — together with the Customer identity stack and the separate \"Citizen\" cookie scheme it runs on. Optional: reference it only if you want the kit's own citizen accounts. A consumer that already has a citizen identity system takes IpgKit.Web.Pay alone and brings its own. Consume via AddIpgKitCustomer / UseIpgKitCustomer.",
